Subject: Make four-entry inline caches the shipping default

What this does
  Changes the default per-site inline-cache width from one entry to four.
  Explicit `-DJS_IC_ENTRIES=1` builds remain available for controlled
  monomorphic comparisons.

Why we need it
  The composed inline-cache implementation is now validated independently,
  but the release projection still used the narrow configuration while device
  benchmark recipes used four entries. This patch makes the shipped
  configuration match the selected device configuration.

What it adds
  Four-entry inline-cache default  - enables the already-ported 0016 width-
                                   configurable cache without changing behavior
                                   or bytecode encoding.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

Notes
  This is a configuration-only follow-up to 0016. The megamorphic threshold
  remains unchanged at eight misses. The foundational width-one configuration
  remains available as an explicit build-time control.

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -310,11 +310,11 @@
-/* JS_IC_ENTRIES is the per-site width. The shipping default remains
-   monomorphic; 0016 can set it to 4 explicitly at compile time. */
+/* JS_IC_ENTRIES is the per-site width. The shipping default is four entries;
+   an explicit -DJS_IC_ENTRIES=1 retains the cheap monomorphic configuration. */
 #ifndef JS_IC_POLY
 #define JS_IC_POLY 0
 #endif
 #ifndef JS_IC_ENTRIES
 #if JS_IC_POLY
 #define JS_IC_ENTRIES 2
 #else
-#define JS_IC_ENTRIES 1
+#define JS_IC_ENTRIES 4
 #endif
 #endif
